---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageGuide from '../components/PageGuide.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { pageGuides } from '../data/page-guides';

const official = {
  overview: 'https://www.europarl.europa.eu/committees/en/cont/discharge-procedure/discharge-2024',
  resolution: 'https://www.europarl.europa.eu/doceo/document/TA-10-2026-0125_EN.html',
  press: 'https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/press-room/20260423IPR41842/',
  agenda: 'https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/agenda/plenary-news/2026-04-27/15/discharge-meps-to-assess-eu-budget-management-in-2024',
  commissionFollowUp: 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52025DC0373',
  courtFollowUp: 'https://www.europarl.europa.eu/cmsdata/297280/Follow-up%20to%20the%20observations%20or%20recommendations%20in%20the%20resolution%20the%20EP%202023%20D.pdf',
  article319: 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A12012E319',
  financialRegulation: 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2509/2024-09-26/eng'
};
---

<Layout title="Budget discharge and institutional follow-up" description="European Parliament budgetary discharge decisions, institutional responses and follow-up documents linked to their official sources.">
  <div class="page discharge-page">
    <header class="page-head discharge-hero">
      <div>
        <h1>Discharge, responses and follow-up</h1>
        <p class="eyebrow">European Parliament · budget accountability</p>
        <p class="lede">A clear record of how Parliament scrutinises EU budget execution, what it decided for 2024 and where to find the institutions’ replies and follow-up work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="discharge-stamp" aria-label="Latest cycle: 2024 budget discharge decided 29 April 2026">
        <span>Latest cycle</span>
        <strong>FY2024</strong>
        <time datetime="2026-04-29">29 Apr 2026</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <PageGuide {...pageGuides.discharge} />

    <nav class="jump" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#latest">Latest decision</a>
      <a href="#responses">FY2023 follow-up</a>
      <a href="#how-it-works">How discharge works</a>
      <a href="#coverage">Coverage note</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="discharge-section" id="latest" aria-labelledby="latest-heading">
      <header class="discharge-section-head">
        <div>
          <h2 id="latest-heading">The 2024 budget discharge</h2>
          <p class="eyebrow">Decision adopted · 29 April 2026</p>
        </div>
        <p>The vote is the newest point in the cycle. It concerns budget management in 2024; the follow-up material below concerns the previous year.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="discharge-status-grid">
        <article class="discharge-status discharge-status-positive">
          <p class="status-kicker">Commission</p>
          <h3>Discharge granted</h3>
          <p>Parliament approved the Commission’s management of the 2024 budget by <strong>389 votes to 255, with 3 abstentions</strong>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="discharge-status discharge-status-hold">
          <p class="status-kicker">Council</p>
          <h3>Decision postponed</h3>
          <p>The Council did not cooperate with the discharge procedure, so Parliament postponed its decision on the Council’s 2024 budget.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="discharge-context"><strong>Across the 2024 cycle:</strong> Parliament granted discharge to the other EU bodies; the Council was the exception because it did not cooperate.</p>

      <div class="discharge-docs">
        <h3>Official material for this cycle</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cycle overview:</strong> <a href={official.overview} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Parliament’s discharge 2024 file<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a></li>
          <li><strong>Adopted act:</strong> <a href={official.resolution} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Commission discharge resolution, 2024 budget (2025/2145(DEC))<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a></li>
          <li><strong>Vote context:</strong> <a href={official.press} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Parliament press release on the discharge votes<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a> and <a href={official.agenda} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">plenary agenda background<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="discharge-section" id="responses" aria-labelledby="responses-heading">
      <header class="discharge-section-head">
        <div>
          <h2 id="responses-heading">Follow-up and institutional replies</h2>
          <p class="eyebrow">Previous cycle · FY2023</p>
        </div>
        <p>These are published responses to Parliament’s FY2023 observations. They are earlier-cycle follow-up, not replies to the FY2024 decision above.</p>
      </header>

      <ul class="discharge-doc-list">
        <li>
          <span class="discharge-doc-type">Commission</span>
          <div>
            <h3><a href={official.commissionFollowUp} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Commission report on follow-up to the 2023 discharge<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a></h3>
            <p>Commission report on measures taken in response to Parliament’s and the Council’s observations and recommendations.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="discharge-doc-type">Court of Justice</span>
          <div>
            <h3><a href={official.courtFollowUp} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Court of Justice follow-up to the 2023 discharge resolution<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a></h3>
            <p>The Court reports on steps taken in response to observations concerning its own budget and administration.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="discharge-doc-type">Index</span>
          <div>
            <h3><a href={official.overview} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Discharge 2024 overview and document index<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span><Icon name="external" size={16} /></a></h3>
            <p>The Parliament committee page gathers the 2024 accounts, European Court of Auditors material, Council recommendations, commissioner replies and follow-up links.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="discharge-section discharge-explainer" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
      <header class="discharge-section-head">
        <div>
          <h2 id="how-heading">What “discharge” means</h2>
          <p class="eyebrow">A short explainer</p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="discharge-explainer-grid">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Budgetary discharge is Parliament’s annual political scrutiny of how EU money was managed and implemented. Parliament reviews the accounts, audit findings, recommendations and the responsible institutions’ answers before deciding whether to grant, postpone or refuse discharge.</p>
          <p>Article 319(3) TFEU requires the Commission to take appropriate steps on observations in discharge decisions and to report on those measures when requested. The Financial Regulation sets the follow-up framework and its timetable. Read the <a href={official.article319} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Treaty provision<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span></a> and <a href={official.financialRegulation} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Financial Regulation 2024/2509<span class="sr-only"> (opens the official source in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
          <p>It is a budget accountability process. It is separate from staff or employment procedures, and a discharge decision does not by itself establish that every irregularity has been resolved.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="discharge-steps" aria-label="Discharge cycle">
          <li><strong>Evidence</strong><span>Accounts, audit findings and recommendations are assembled.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Answers</strong><span>Institutions provide replies and supporting follow-up material.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Decision</strong><span>Parliament grants, postpones or refuses discharge.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Follow-up</strong><span>Later reports track responses and outstanding requests.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <p class="notice discharge-timing"><Icon name="info" /><span>Timing matters: the FY2024 decision is recorded above, while the linked detailed responses here are from the FY2023 follow-up cycle. This page does not infer that a FY2024 follow-up response has already been published.</span></p>
    </section>

    <section class="discharge-section discharge-note" id="coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-heading">
      <h2 id="coverage-heading">Coverage and source note</h2>
      <p>This page is a small editorial guide to official discharge material from the European Parliament, Commission and Court of Justice, checked on <time datetime="2026-10-02">2 October 2026</time>. The linked documents are the authority; this page summarises their status and separates the newest decision from earlier follow-up responses.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
